From: postmarketOS realme-lunaa port
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: send an UNBLANK panel notification from
 dsi_display_enable()

The panel blank notifications this tree sends to the touchscreen driver are
asymmetric: the POWERDOWN half is emitted from the generic DRM path, the
UNBLANK half only from an OPlus-specific one.

  - dsi_display_disable() emits MSM_DRM_BLANK_POWERDOWN (EARLY_EVENT_BLANK on
    entry, EVENT_BLANK on exit), on both the msm_drm and drm_panel chains.
  - dsi_display_enable() emits nothing at all.
  - The only MSM_DRM_BLANK_UNBLANK on the drm_panel chain comes from
    dsi_display_oplus_set_power() (techpack/display/oplus/
    oplus_display_private_api.c), reached via _sde_connector_update_power_locked()
    when the legacy DRM DPMS connector property changes.
  - The generic notifier call in sde_kms.c that would have covered both
    directions is compiled out under #ifndef OPLUS_BUG_STABILITY.

Android's HWC sets that DPMS property, so downstream never notices. wlroots
has been atomic-only since 0.18: it toggles CRTC ACTIVE and never touches the
legacy property, so on a mainline-userspace distribution the UNBLANK is never
sent.

The oplus touchscreen driver registers on the drm_panel chain
(touchpanel_common_driver.c, CONFIG_DRM_OPLUS_PANEL_NOTIFY branch) and drives
tp_suspend()/tp_resume() from it. The result is that the first screen blank
suspends the touch controller and nothing ever resumes it -- the panel comes
back, but the touchscreen is dead until reboot, with no error anywhere:

  [   93.506928] [TP0]touchpanel: fb_notifier_callback: event = 2, blank = 1
  [   93.637229] [TP0]touchpanel: fb_notifier_callback: event = 1, blank = 1
  [   93.637232] [TP0]touchpanel: tp_suspend: start.
  [   93.644814] [TP0]touchpanel: tp_suspend: end.
  <screen switched back on -- nothing further is logged>

Mirror dsi_display_disable(): send EARLY_EVENT_BLANK/UNBLANK on the way in and
EVENT_BLANK/UNBLANK on the way out, on both chains.

The early notification is placed after the continuous-splash block rather than
at the top of the function. That block has two early returns of its own, and
sending EARLY without a matching EVENT is not harmless: under
tp_resume_order == LCD_TP_RESUME, lcd_on_early_event() calls
disable_irq_nosync() and only lcd_on_event() re-enables it. Below the block,
every path that sends EARLY also reaches the exit label that sends EVENT.

--- a/techpack/display/msm/dsi/dsi_display.c	2026-08-26 19:03:31.401959882 +0300
+++ b/techpack/display/msm/dsi/dsi_display.c	2026-08-26 19:04:37.831300922 +0300
@@ -8897,6 +8897,10 @@
 {
 	int rc = 0;
 	struct dsi_display_mode *mode;
+#ifdef CONFIG_DRM_OPLUS_PANEL_NOTIFY
+	int blank;
+	struct msm_drm_notifier notifier_data;
+#endif
 
 	if (!display || !display->panel) {
 		DSI_ERR("Invalid params\n");
@@ -8943,6 +8947,17 @@
 		return 0;
 	}
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_DRM_OPLUS_PANEL_NOTIFY
+	blank = MSM_DRM_BLANK_UNBLANK;
+	notifier_data.data = &blank;
+	notifier_data.id = 0;
+	msm_drm_notifier_call_chain(MSM_DRM_EARLY_EVENT_BLANK,
+					&notifier_data);
+	drm_panel_notifier_call_chain(&display->panel->drm_panel,
+					MSM_DRM_EARLY_EVENT_BLANK,
+					&notifier_data);
+#endif
+
 	mutex_lock(&display->display_lock);
 
 	mode = display->panel->cur_mode;
@@ -9036,6 +9051,14 @@
 	}
 #endif
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_DRM_OPLUS_PANEL_NOTIFY
+	msm_drm_notifier_call_chain(MSM_DRM_EVENT_BLANK,
+					&notifier_data);
+	drm_panel_notifier_call_chain(&display->panel->drm_panel,
+					MSM_DRM_EVENT_BLANK,
+					&notifier_data);
+#endif
+
 	SDE_EVT32(SDE_EVTLOG_FUNC_EXIT);
 	return rc;
 }
